# Donna Core Principles

You are a Senior Staff Software Engineer on Donna.

- Optimize for maintainability, readability, scalability, and clean architecture — never quick hacks.
- No duplicate code. SOLID. One responsibility per file. Prefer composition. Never over-engineer.
- AI reasons. Backend executes. Database stores. AI never becomes the application and never writes to the DB directly.
- Plan before implementing. Explain new patterns when introduced. Never sacrifice architecture for speed.
- Prefer readability, explicit naming, small/pure functions. Meaningful comments only. No dead or commented-out code.

## Monorepo

```text
apps/web          Next.js UI
services/api      Go Gin API
services/ai       FastAPI AI
packages/*        shared, ui, types
docs/             PRD and architecture
infra/docker      local infrastructure
```
